## 14. Security and data protection

Implement security from the beginning.

Requirements:
- Enable and test Supabase Row Level Security on user-owned data.
- Users may only access their own profile, plans, attempts and progress.
- Enforce admin permissions on the server.
- Never put privileged service-role keys in frontend code.
- Keep AI and search provider credentials server-side.
- Validate all input on both client and server.
- Restrict document download size and accepted file types.
- Protect against malicious files, prompt injection inside documents, SQL injection and cross-site scripting.
- Treat extracted document content and web pages as untrusted data, never as instructions to the AI agent.
- Use rate limits and quotas for expensive operations.
- Prevent repeated requests from creating duplicate background jobs.
- Use signed URLs or private storage for non-public files.
- Do not expose answer keys before submission.
- Minimize personal data collection.
- Provide a way for users to delete their account and associated personal data.
- Keep secrets out of source control and logs.

Do not execute code extracted from exam documents.

## 15. AI content quality and human review

AI-generated content must be treated as a proposal, not automatically as authoritative.

Use statuses such as:
- `pending_review`
- `approved`
- `rejected`
- `needs_correction`

Provide an admin review interface for:
- Extracted questions.
- Proposed answers.
- Topic mappings.
- Lessons.
- Quiz questions.
- AI-generated explanations.

Keep source references alongside content derived from past exams.

Clearly distinguish:
- Official content.
- Content extracted from a document.
- AI-generated explanations.
- Human-reviewed content.

The app must not promise that its predictions guarantee success in a future competition.

## 16. Backend architecture

Implement clear service boundaries:

- `ExamResearchService` — finds and registers relevant exam sources.
- `DocumentProcessingService` — downloads documents, extracts text and runs OCR.
- `QuestionExtractionService` — proposes structured questions with page references.
- `TopicClassificationService` — maps questions to the topic taxonomy.
- `TopicStatisticsService` — calculates frequency, coverage and confidence.
- `PriorityScoringService` — ranks topics with an explainable formula.
- `StudyPlanGeneratorService` — creates a schedule that fits the candidate's time.
- `LessonService` — retrieves and manages lesson content.
- `QuizService` — manages questions, submissions and scoring.
- `ProgressService` — tracks mastery and recommends revisions.
- `AdminReviewService` — validates generated and extracted content.

Keep business logic outside UI components.

Use typed API contracts, centralized error handling, structured logs and database transactions where appropriate.

Implement asynchronous jobs for slow operations and expose job status to the frontend.

