## 18. Implementation phases

Build the application in phases. At the end of each phase, run tests, fix errors and update the documentation.

### Phase 1 — Project foundation and UI
- Inspect the repository.
- Set up the frontend and backend architecture.
- Create the design system and responsive layouts.
- Implement navigation and onboarding.
- Add environment-variable validation.
- Provide a working landing page and onboarding flow.

### Phase 2 — Database and authentication
- Create schema migrations.
- Implement registration and login.
- Configure Row Level Security.
- Test user isolation.
- Add profiles and candidate preferences.

### Phase 3 — Exam sources and documents
- Create the source catalog.
- Add a small set of verified, publicly accessible seed sources.
- Implement document ingestion, deduplication and extraction.
- Track processing status, provenance and errors.
- Add an admin page to manage sources and documents.

### Phase 4 — Topic classification and statistics
- Create the topic taxonomy.
- Implement structured question extraction.
- Add AI-assisted classification behind a provider abstraction.
- Calculate topic frequency and coverage from actual processed documents.
- Display confidence and sample size.
- Add tests for all calculations.

### Phase 5 — Dynamic study plans
- Implement priority scoring.
- Generate plans using specialty, level, duration, hours per day and target competition.
- Persist plans and their source evidence.
- Display daily tasks and reasons for prioritization.
- Verify that the plan fits the available time.

### Phase 6 — Lessons and quizzes
- Build lesson pages and exercises.
- Implement chapter-specific quizzes.
- Add scoring and detailed corrections.
- Protect answer keys.
- Connect study activities to the daily plan.

### Phase 7 — Progress and adaptive revision
- Add progress dashboards.
- Track quiz history and topic mastery.
- Recommend revisions.
- Adapt remaining tasks without deleting completed work.

### Phase 8 — Administration, quality and deployment
- Complete content-review workflows.
- Add security, integration and end-to-end tests.
- Improve accessibility and mobile layouts.
- Add logging and operational documentation.
- Prepare deployment instructions and production environment configuration.

Do not skip ahead while a phase has unresolved critical errors.

