## 20. Definition of done

The first production-minded version is complete only when:

1. A candidate can register and save their profile.
2. They can select a specialty, level, preparation duration and daily availability.
3. The application can retrieve or use verified exam documents from its configured source catalog.
4. The system extracts questions with source and page references where possible.
5. Topic frequencies are calculated from actual processed documents.
6. Missing evidence and uncertain AI output are clearly identified.
7. The application generates a personalized plan that fits the candidate's available time.
8. The candidate can study a chapter and take a test on that chapter.
9. Quiz answers are scored securely and corrections are displayed.
10. Progress is saved and future revision recommendations use the candidate's results.
11. Users cannot access one another's private data.
12. Administrative permissions are enforced on the backend.
13. Automated tests pass.
14. The application can be deployed using documented instructions.
15. A developer can run the application locally by following the README.

